    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d989">

                <pb facs="1041" n="755" xml:id="pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/3826</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >McAdoo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 22</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to your letter
                    requesting that the collectors of customs be instructed to make report upon a
                    merchant vessel’s armament each time the vessel arrives.</p>
                <p>This Department notices that this course results, especially in the case of
                    liners arriving at New York, in many duplicate reports, since on each trip the
                    pertinent facts are substantially the same.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to inform me, therefore, whether it will not suffice for the
                    purposes of your Department to have reports made and specify authority for
                    clearance requested only when there is some material change in the armament,
                    etc., from what has already been reported on a preceding arrival of the same
                    vessel.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Secretary.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Peters</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
